# Final whole-branch review findings (base 1d38033, head 365b340)

Verdict: Ready to merge. 0 Critical, 0 Important, 2 Minor. This wave fixes both.

## Finding 1 (Minor): wrong co-author trailer on commit 365b340
Location: commit 365b340 "feat: add readingTimeMinutes" (current HEAD, unpushed).
Issue: its trailer reads `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; every other branch commit and the session attribution use `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.
Recommendation: reword that one commit message so the trailer reads `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`. Change nothing else in the message or the tree.

## Finding 2 (Minor): tie-break test cannot distinguish `<`/`>` from localeCompare
Location: test/topWords.test.js:130-133 (tie-break test), src/textstats.js:116 (comparison).
Issue: the test uses only lowercase ASCII words, so it passes whether ties are ordered by code-unit comparison (`<`/`>`, what the plan specifies) or by `localeCompare`. The plan's tie-order rule is effectively untested.
Recommendation: add an assertion such as
`assert.deepEqual(topWords('zebra éclair', 5).map(e => e.word), ['zebra', 'éclair']);`
Code-unit order puts z (U+007A) before é (U+00E9); localeCompare would put éclair first.

## Fix notes (fixer appends below)
